# ============================================================================
# SENSITIVE FILES - NEVER COMMIT TO GIT
# ============================================================================

# Environment variables with API keys (CRITICAL - contains secrets!)
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.development
*.env

# Exception: Allow .env.example template (contains only placeholders)
!.env.example

# .env.example2 — contains real API keys, never commit
.env.example2

# Docs/ is local only, in full. Design notes, port packs, handover
# documents, deployment playbooks, health reports and the production
# playbook all stay on the machine that wrote them. Nothing under Docs/
# is tracked, and there is deliberately no negation rule here: if one
# file needs to travel between trees it belongs at the repo root, not in
# Docs/. The playbook in particular names the live server IP and the
# root SSH target, and this repo is published to a public remote.
Docs/

# Forensic reports naming the production server's origin IP.
.aiwg/

# Local working notes at the repo root. Each one is written for a single
# machine and a single session: the project health snapshot, a dated debug
# write-up, and the agent instruction file. No code reads them. The agent's
# rules loader reads AGENTS.md (~/.cortex/AGENTS.md, .cortex/AGENTS.md, or the
# repo root), never CLAUDE.md, so a clone without these is complete and
# builds and runs exactly the same.
#
# Every rule here is anchored with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored
# CLAUDE.md would also swallow any nested file of that name; only the root
# copies are local-only. There is deliberately no negation rule.
/CLAUDE.md
/PROJECT_INDEX.md
/CHAT_STUCK_ISSUES_2026-10-27.md

# ============================================================================
# Python Environment & Dependencies
# ============================================================================

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python packages
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
# The whole build/ tree, build/linux/ included. The packaging scripts are
# release tooling kept on the machine that builds a release; they are not
# source, and a fresh clone no longer produces an installer on its own.
/build/

# ============================================================================
# IDE & Editor Files
# ============================================================================

# VS Code
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

opencode/

# PyCharm
.idea/
*.iml

# Qoder
.qoder/

# Cortex config (may contain sensitive paths)
.cortex/
.backup.src/


# ============================================================================
# Logs & Temporary Files
# ============================================================================

# Log files
*.log
logs/
test_out.txt

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
nul
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ============================================================================
# Test Files
# ============================================================================

# The whole tests/ tree stays out of the repository. The files remain on
# disk for local runs; git simply does not carry them.
#
# There must be NO `!tests/**` negation anywhere in this file. A negation
# placed after this rule re-includes the tree and silently defeats it.
/tests/

# Stray one-off test scripts at the repo ROOT only.
# Must stay anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `test_*.py` matches
# at EVERY depth, which silently swallowed the entire tests/ package —
# `git add tests/` reported success and committed nothing.
/test_*.py
clear_deepseek_key.py
fix_deepseek_key.py
reset_settings.py

# Test cache
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
coverage/
.htmlcov/

# ============================================================================
# Build Artifacts & Installer Output
# ============================================================================

# PyInstaller onedir output and packaged artifacts
dist/
*.spec

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build machinery -- kept out of the repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Specs, installer scripts and packaging helpers are release tooling that
# lives on the machine doing the build, not source. They are no longer
# tracked, so a published clone carries no installer definitions.
# *.spec a few lines up already covers every PyInstaller spec, and /build/ is
# ignored as a whole tree; these are the remaining pieces that need naming.
/build_tools/
/build.ps1
/cortex_setup.iss

# Inno Setup
installer_output/
*.exe
*.dll
*.pak
*.bin
# The installer script is release tooling, not source. Kept on the build
# machine and never tracked (also named in the block above).
cortex_setup.iss

# ============================================================================
# Node.js & Frontend
# ============================================================================

# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# External repos
opencode-dev/
vscode-main/
claude-code/

